; Fiber context-switch primitives (self-scaling stage 1, milestone 1.1).
;
; Implemented in vendored assembly under fiber/ (fcontext_arm64.S AAPCS64,
; fcontext_x86_64.S SysV — the two ABIs covering all four LP64 targets),
; Boost.Context fcontext style: a context is a stack pointer to a frame of
; callee-saved registers. tools/fcontext.sh assembles the host's file with
; clang; every libscaly.a build archives the object alongside libscaly.o.
;
; API (no transfer_t struct return): the resumed side receives the JUMPER's
; fresh context in the first argument register — a fresh context's entry
; function gets it as its argument, a suspended context gets it as
; scaly_jump_context's return value. An entry function must never return
; (it traps); fiber completion arrives with the scheduler in milestone 1.3.
;
; Unreferenced by the scaly package itself, so these emit no `declare` into
; scaly.ll (fixpoint-safe, same pattern as memory/runtime.scaly's read).

function scaly_make_context(stack_top: pointer[void], fn: pointer[void]) returns pointer[void] extern
procedure scaly_jump_context(to: pointer[void]) returns pointer[void] extern
